    14	
    15	# Feature: Guardrails
    16	
    17	The 13 Iron Laws plus the mistake-capture-and-learn loop that keep agents in scope, verifying claims, and not repeating known traps. This is one of the 7 capability value-features the memory-system redesign ratified (memory-system-redesign design doc §1.2). Iron Law #13 (no document work without a spec and a CRUD plan) is the principle this feature most recently added.
    18	
    19	## Overview
    20	
    21	`guardrails` unites gobbi's behavioral floor (the Iron Laws) with its learning loop (mistake capture and two-layer promotion): together they keep agents inside scope, verifying before claiming done, and not repeating known traps across sessions.
    22	
    23	## Status
    24	
    25	Active. The behavioral floor (13 Iron Laws in the `principles` skill) and the mistake-capture loop (the `mistake` skill plus the `mistakes/` tier) are both live. The feature directory itself was created during the memory-system redesign when work-sprint artifacts were re-homed into the 7 capability value-features; durable guardrails artifacts (cross-layer drift gating and hook-event documentation references) now live under this directory's subdirectories.
    26	
    27	## Subsystems
    28	
    29	- `principles` (the 13 Iron Laws, incl. new #13)
    30	- `mistake` (moment-of-capture, two-layer promotion, required-mistakes wiring) + the `mistakes/` tier as consumer
    31	
    32	## Subdirectories
    33	
    34	- `decisions/` — guardrails design decisions
    35	- `design/` — guardrails-scope design topics
    36	- `discussions/` — substantive AskUserQuestion topics scoped to guardrails
    37	- `references/` — external prior art touching principles / mistakes
    38	- `plans/` — plan artifacts produced by the Planning loop
    39	- `changelogs/` — what shipped per task
    40	- `archive/` — superseded guardrails artifacts (move-on-terminal)
    41	
    42	## Recent activity
    43	
    44	| Date | Session | What |
    45	|---|---|---|
    46	| 2026-05-26 | a10c82d6 | Feature directory created during the memory-system redesign and seeded with re-homed work-sprint artifacts |
    47	
    48	## Open items
    49	
    50	- Correct the "31 hook events" claim to the verified count of 29 in surviving references — see `backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md`.
    51	- Empirically re-verify the `PostToolUseFailure` hook contract when authoring its `.claude/settings.json` registration — see `backlogs/posttooluse-failure-webfetch-verification-gap.md`.
    52	- Add a quality gate on `agents[]` field population if presence is ever treated as a metric — see `backlogs/goodhart-factor-when-demanded-deferred.md`.
