    16	
    17	# Claude Code lifecycle events for hooks
    18	
    19	## Insight
    20	Claude Code now provides 12+ hook lifecycle events. The relevant ones for subagent telemetry are:
    21	
    22	| Event | Triggers when | Available for shell command hooks (.claude/settings.json)? |
    23	|---|---|---|
    24	| `PreToolUse` | A tool call is about to fire | Yes |
    25	| `PostToolUse` | A tool call succeeded | Yes |
    26	| `PostToolUseFailure` | A tool call failed | Yes |
    27	| `SubagentStart` | Subagent initialization | SDK only (Python + TypeScript) |
    28	| `SubagentStop` | Subagent completion | SDK only — Stop hooks are automatically converted to SubagentStop when running inside a subagent |
    29	| `SessionStart` | Session initialization | TypeScript SDK or `.claude/settings.json` shell command |
    30	| `SessionEnd` | Session termination | TypeScript SDK or `.claude/settings.json` shell command (Python SDK lacks this) |
    31	
    32	PostToolUse + the matcher pattern `"Task"` is the shell-command-hook-compatible path for "fire after every Agent spawn." `SubagentStop` is a richer event but is SDK-only, which means it requires running gobbi through the agent SDK rather than the standalone Claude Code CLI — a heavier integration than the current `.claude/settings.json` `hooks.*` configuration model.
    33	
    34	A v2.1.119 addition: `PostToolUse` and `PostToolUseFailure` hook inputs now include `duration_ms` — tool execution time excluding permission prompts and PreToolUse hook execution.
    35	
    36	## Related
    37	
    38	- `claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md` (the companion reference with the full PostToolUse / PostToolUseFailure input schema)
    39	- `checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md` (the drift gate that keeps hook registration aligned across `.claude/settings.json`, skills, and the session schema)
    40	
    41	## Why it applies
    42	The subagent-telemetry hook design picks PostToolUse + matcher `"Task"` as its mechanism. This reference establishes:
    43	1. PostToolUse is the **shell-command-compatible** event for subagent completion telemetry — consistent with the existing `session-start.sh` shell-script precedent.
    44	2. SubagentStop is a richer alternative but requires SDK integration that gobbi does not currently use — out of scope.
    45	3. PostToolUse has matured (v2.1.119 added `duration_ms`) — the schema is in active evolution, so the hook script should be defensive about field availability.
    46	4. `PostToolUseFailure` is the parallel event for failed tool calls — the hook design should consider whether failed subagent spawns also populate `agents[]` (probably yes, with a `status` field reflecting failure).
    47	
    48	## Source
    49	- https://claudefa.st/blog/tools/hooks/hooks-guide
    50	- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks (referenced)
    51	- Both accessed 2026-05-23
    52	
    53	## Excerpt
    54	> "PostToolUse duration (v2.1.119): PostToolUse and PostToolUseFailure hook inputs now include duration_ms — tool execution time in milliseconds, excluding time spent in permission prompts and PreToolUse hook execution, available on both PostToolUse and PostToolUseFailure hooks."
    55	> "For subagents, Stop hooks are automatically converted to SubagentStop since that is the event that fires when a subagent completes."
    56	
    57	## Usage history
    58	
    59	| Date | Session | Used for |
    60	|---|---|---|
    61	| 2026-05-23 | 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac | Mapped the hook lifecycle landscape for the subagent-telemetry design; ruled out SubagentStop for the shell-command path; flagged PostToolUseFailure for failed-spawn coverage |

