    10	tags: [hook, posttooluse, posttooluse-failure, agent-tool, schema, telemetry]
    11	title: Claude Code PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure hook — official input schema + empirical Task tool payload
    12	source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks
    13	accessed: 2026-05-23
    14	ref_type: docs
    15	---
    16	
    17	# Claude Code PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure hooks — official schema
    18	
    19	## Insight
    20	PostToolUse fires **after a tool call succeeds**; PostToolUseFailure fires **after a tool call fails**. Both pipe a JSON payload to stdin with these fields:
    21	- **Common:** `session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `effort`, `hook_event_name` (= `"PostToolUse"` or `"PostToolUseFailure"`), optional `agent_id` + `agent_type` (populated when the hook fires inside a subagent).
    22	- **Tool-specific:** `tool_name`, `tool_input` (the input parameters sent to the tool), `tool_use_id` (unique id correlating PreToolUse/PostToolUse pairs), `tool_result` (the result/output; for PostToolUseFailure this carries the failure payload).
    23	- **Recent additions (v2.1.119+):** `duration_ms` — tool execution time excluding permission prompts / PreToolUse hook execution.
    24	
    25	Matcher patterns support exact string ("Bash"), pipe-separated alternation ("Edit|Write"), regex ("^Notebook"), and MCP-tool patterns ("mcp__memory__.*"). The matcher pattern `"Task"` is the canonical target for hooks that want to fire after subagent spawns.
    26	
    27	The hook's `tool_result` payload schema for Task/Agent calls is documented less rigorously than the common fields. The official `tool_result` example in the docs is a simple `{"type": "text", "text": "..."}`. However, the agent-SDK doc (a sibling doc) describes the **TaskOutput** interface as `{result: string, usage?: {input_tokens, output_tokens}, total_cost_usd?, duration_ms?}` for the Task tool. Multiple secondary sources state empirically that "PostToolUse `tool_response` for a completed Agent call carries the subagent's final text along with usage telemetry." Token usage is at least partially observable; the exact shape depends on Claude Code version.
    28	
    29	The hook **also receives `transcript_path`** in every fire — meaning a hook can read the transcript JSONL itself and extract the rich `toolUseResult` payload that Claude Code writes (which contains the full subagent metadata: agentId, agentType, totalDurationMs, totalTokens, totalToolUseCount, usage{input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens, output_tokens}, toolStats{readCount, searchCount, bashCount, editFileCount, linesAdded, linesRemoved}).
    30	
    31	## Related
    32	
    33	- `claude-code-hooks-12-lifecycle-events.md` (the companion reference covering the broader hook lifecycle-event landscape)
    34	- `checklists/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md` and `backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md` (the tracked docs-sync item: the "31 events" claim below should be corrected to the verified count of 29)
    35	- `backlogs/posttooluse-failure-webfetch-verification-gap.md` (the deferred empirical re-verification of the verbatim quotes captured here)
    36	
    37	## PostToolUseFailure — verbatim verification
    38	
    39	WebFetched `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` on 2026-05-23. The official docs page lists `PostToolUseFailure` as one of 31 documented hook events and includes it in two tables:
    40	
    41	**Lifecycle table (verbatim):**
    42	
    43	> | Event                 | When it fires                                                                                                                                          |
    44	> | :-------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
    45	> | `PostToolUseFailure`  | After a tool call fails                                                                                                                                |
    46	
    47	**Exit-code behavior table (verbatim):**
    48	
    49	> | Hook event            | Can block? | What happens on exit 2                                                                                               |
    50	> | :-------------------- | :--------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
    51	> | `PostToolUseFailure`  | No         | Shows stderr to Claude (tool already failed)                                                                         |
    52	
    53	Shell-command hook support is explicitly confirmed: PostToolUseFailure supports the same `type: "command"` registration shape as PostToolUse (alongside HTTP, MCP-tool, prompt, and agent hooks). It is non-blocking — exit code 2 does not prevent the underlying tool failure but does surface the hook's stderr to Claude.
    54	
    55	All 31 documented hook events on this page (full enumeration for context):
    56	
    57	1. `SessionStart`
    58	2. `Setup`
    59	3. `UserPromptSubmit`
    60	4. `UserPromptExpansion`
    61	5. `PreToolUse`
    62	6. `PermissionRequest`
    63	7. `PermissionDenied`
    64	8. `PostToolUse`
    65	9. `PostToolUseFailure`
    66	10. `PostToolBatch`
    67	11. `Notification`
    68	12. `SubagentStart`
    69	13. `SubagentStop`
    70	14. `TaskCreated`
    71	15. `TaskCompleted`
    72	16. `Stop`
    73	17. `StopFailure`
    74	18. `TeammateIdle`
    75	19. `InstructionsLoaded`
    76	20. `ConfigChange`
    77	21. `CwdChanged`
    78	22. `FileChanged`
    79	23. `WorktreeCreate`
    80	24. `WorktreeRemove`
    81	25. `PreCompact`
    82	26. `PostCompact`
    83	27. `Elicitation`
    84	28. `ElicitationResult`
    85	29. `SessionEnd`
    86	
    87	(The page's table lists 31; the enumerated names above cover the explicitly captured events from the same WebFetch.)
    88	
    89	## Why it applies
    90	The subagent-telemetry hook design explicitly required verifying the hook contract before committing to the mechanism. This insight is the verification answer:
    91	- The hook fires after every Agent tool call (matcher `"Task"`).
    92	- The hook receives `tool_name`, `tool_input` (subagent_type, prompt, model, description), `tool_result` (basic), and `transcript_path` (the route to the rich payload).
    93	- If hook input alone is insufficient, the hook can `jq` the transcript file to extract the full `toolUseResult` block (verified empirically during the guardrails Ideation: the transcript JSONL carries the rich subagent metadata enumerated in the Insight section above).
    94	- **PostToolUseFailure** is officially supported for shell-command hooks (verbatim quote above), so the dual registration (PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure) is grounded in the official documentation, not in community attestation.
    95	
    96	This gives the design a clear path: even if `tool_result` in the hook payload is impoverished, the hook is rich enough because `transcript_path` is always provided. The design's mechanism — a hook for real-time append plus a shell-script reconstructor for repair — is fully supported, and the dual-event (success + failure) registration is officially documented.
    97	
    98	## Source
    99	- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks
   100	- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/hooks
   101	- Both accessed 2026-05-23
   102	
   103	## Excerpt
   104	> "PostToolUse | After a tool call succeeds"
   105	> "PostToolUseFailure | After a tool call fails"
   106	> "Common Fields (all hooks): `session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `effort`, `hook_event_name`. Optional: `agent_id` and `agent_type` (when running in a subagent)."
   107	> "Tool-Specific Fields: `tool_name`, `tool_input`, `tool_use_id`, `tool_result`."
   108	> "**Yes, matchers work for PostToolUse.** You can filter by tool name using patterns… Pipe-separated list `\"Edit|Write\"` | Either tool exactly"
   109	> "PostToolUseFailure | No | Shows stderr to Claude (tool already failed)"
   110	
   111	## Usage history
   112	
   113	| Date | Session | Used for |
   114	|---|---|---|
   115	| 2026-05-23 | 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac | Closed the hook-contract verification gate for the PostToolUse-based subagent telemetry design |
   116	| 2026-05-23 | 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac | Added the verbatim PostToolUseFailure quote to ground the dual-event hook registration in the official docs |

