    17	
    18	# Empirical toolUseResult payload — Claude Code transcript JSONL shape
    19	
    20	## Insight
    21	The Claude Code transcript JSONL contains a top-level `toolUseResult` field on every tool-result line corresponding to an Agent (Task) tool call. The shape — empirically verified from a real session transcript — is:
    22	
    23	```json
    24	{
    25	  "status": "completed",
    26	  "prompt": "<full delegation prompt text passed to the subagent>",
    27	  "agentId": "<subagent session id>",
    28	  "agentType": "leader" | "executor" | "evaluator" | "assistant",
    29	  "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<subagent's final response>"}],
    30	  "totalDurationMs": <number>,
    31	  "totalTokens": <number>,
    32	  "totalToolUseCount": <number>,
    33	  "usage": {
    34	    "input_tokens": <number>,
    35	    "cache_creation_input_tokens": <number>,
    36	    "cache_read_input_tokens": <number>,
    37	    "output_tokens": <number>,
    38	    "server_tool_use": {...},
    39	    "service_tier": "standard",
    40	    "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": <number>, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": <number>},
    41	    "inference_geo": "",
    42	    "iterations": [...],
    43	    "speed": "standard"
    44	  },
    45	  "toolStats": {
    46	    "readCount": <number>,
    47	    "searchCount": <number>,
    48	    "bashCount": <number>,
    49	    "editFileCount": <number>,
    50	    "linesAdded": <number>,
    51	    "linesRemoved": <number>,
    52	    "otherToolCount": <number>
    53	  }
    54	}
    55	```
    56	
    57	Method: read `$CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH` JSONL, find the line where `toolUseResult.agentId == <subagent-id>` (or correlate by `tool_use_id` against the preceding tool_use line), extract every field above. Every field in `session.template.json.agents[]` is satisfiable from this single payload:
    58	
    59	| session.template.json field | toolUseResult source |
    60	|---|---|
    61	| `id` | `agentId` |
    62	| `name` | derive from `agentType` + spawn description (in tool_input.description) |
    63	| `type` | `agentType` |
    64	| `step` / `phase` / `iter` | NOT in toolUseResult — must be supplied by the manager via the delegation prompt's metadata OR reconstructed by parsing the prompt body |
    65	| `model` | NOT in toolUseResult — must be supplied from the `tool_use.input.model` field (line 164 in the transcript) |
    66	| `system` | always `claude-code` for native Agent calls; `codex` for codex tool calls |
    67	| `transcriptPath` | the parent session's transcriptPath (subagent transcripts live as sidechain entries in the same JSONL — flagged via `isSidechain: true`) |
    68	| `tokensUsed.input` | `usage.input_tokens` |
    69	| `tokensUsed.output` | `usage.output_tokens` |
    70	| `tokensUsed.cacheRead` | `usage.cache_read_input_tokens` |
    71	| `tokensUsed.cacheCreation` | `usage.cache_creation_input_tokens` |
    72	| `startedAt` | timestamp of the preceding tool_use line (line 164) |
    73	| `finishedAt` | timestamp of the tool_result line (line 165) |
    74	
    75	## Why it applies
    76	The PostToolUse hook and shell-script reconstructor both consume from the same authoritative source (transcript JSONL `toolUseResult`). The hook reads the transcript at fire time (using `$CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH` from its stdin), the reconstructor reads at session-end time. The schema gaps surfaced above (`step`, `phase`, `iter`, `model`) inform the design of the delegation prompt structure (these fields must be parseable from the prompt body — e.g., the leader prompt's first three lines already include "Your phase: ideation", "Your iteration: 1", "Your sub-step: C"). This reference demonstrates empirically that per-spawn metadata IS observable from the transcript.
    77	
    78	## Source
    79	- File: `~/.claude/projects/-playinganalytics-git-gobbi/7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068.jsonl`
    80	- Extracted via direct empirical inspection 2026-05-23

